# Single source of truth for the vendored `helm` pin (M29.8a, ADR-0059) — the `apps/runner-dep-vendor`
# sandbox's `helm template` step (Gitea's re-vendor, network-none, credential-free).
#
# Shell-sourceable (`. tools/helm/pin.env`) AND parsed verbatim by:
#   - apps/runner-dep-vendor/Dockerfile   (ARG HELM_PINNED_VERSION / HELM_PINNED_SHA256 defaults)
# `packages/plugins/managed-dep/src/runner-dep-vendor-image.test.ts` asserts the Dockerfile agrees
# with this file, the same drift-test shape as tools/skopeo/pin.env and tools/busybox/pin.env.
#
# WHY A TARBALL + CHECKSUM, NOT A DIGEST-PINNED IMAGE (the deliberate deviation from
# tools/cosign/pin.env, tools/skopeo/pin.env and tools/trivy/pin.env). Those three vendor a binary
# out of the UPSTREAM PROJECT'S OWN published image. Helm publishes no first-party container image at
# all (helm/helm ships only `helm-vX.Y.Z-<os>-<arch>.tar.gz` release assets + a co-published
# `.tar.gz.sha256sum`) — so the pin here is the same shape `apps/runner-iac/Dockerfile`'s header
# explicitly considered and rejected for OpenTofu only because OpenTofu's own image was still usable
# via `COPY --from=<image>` (its ONBUILD block only fires on `FROM`); Helm never had an image to begin
# with. `apps/runner-dep-vendor/Dockerfile` downloads the pinned tarball and verifies it against the
# checksum below BEFORE extracting it — content-addressed the same way a digest pin is, just against
# upstream's own published checksum rather than a registry manifest digest.
#
# HELM 3, NOT HELM 4 (recorded, not an oversight — re-check before bumping past 3.x). Helm 4.0
# shipped 2026-09; `tools/vendor-refresh/src/gitea-plan.ts` was built and tested entirely against
# Helm 3's `helm template` output shape (its Secret/hook-annotation parsing, `# Source:` comment
# stripping). Moving to Helm 4 needs that compatibility re-verified against a real Helm 4 render
# before the pin follows — a separate, deliberate piece of work, not a version bump.

# The exact release this pin corresponds to (matches `helm version --short`'s reported version).
HELM_PINNED_VERSION=v3.16.4

# linux/amd64 only — this repo builds linux/amd64 images exclusively (see apps/runner-iac/Dockerfile's
# own note on the same scope decision).
HELM_PINNED_ARCHIVE=helm-v3.16.4-linux-amd64.tar.gz

# sha256 of the archive above, cross-checked against upstream's own co-published
# `helm-v3.16.4-linux-amd64.tar.gz.sha256sum` at https://get.helm.sh/ (measured 2026-09-25).
HELM_PINNED_SHA256=fc307327959aa38ed8f9f7e66d45492bb022a66c3e5da6063958254b9767d179
